Involves creating and delivering malicious payload to the target system. 
I think it also involves testing the boundaries of a system to detect potential vulnerabilities.
Different XSS types include
REFLECTED XSS
  User supplied data in an HTTP request is included in the webpage source without any validation.
Possible entry points include;
i. Parameters in the URL Query string
ii. URL File Path
Sometimes HTTP headers.

STORED XSS
  Stored on the webapp(Database); it runs when the site is visited. 
Possible entry points
i. Comments on a blog.
ii. User profile info.
iii. Website listings.

BLIND XSS
  Delivers payload to test against yourself.

